<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The interface.

  Where the iOS catalogue exists, the English value here is that catalogue's *key*
  verbatim, so the two platforms read the same and a translator can diff them.
  Counts use plain positional formatting rather than `<plurals>` on purpose: the
  iOS catalogue has no plural rules, and introducing them would make English say
  "1 step" where every other string in this app — and the Chinese translation —
  says "1 steps". Parity over grammar here, deliberately.
-->
